  "instructions": [
    "Toss the chicken strips in a bowl with 1 tbsp olive oil, paprika, cumin, garlic powder, salt, and pepper until evenly coated.",
    "Heat 1 tbsp olive oil in a 12 inch skillet over medium-high heat until it shimmers.",
    "Add the chicken in a single layer. Cook 5 to 6 minutes, stirring once or twice, until browned and no longer pink inside. Move it to a plate.",
    "Add the remaining 1 tbsp olive oil to the skillet. Add the peppers and onion.",
    "Cook 5 to 6 minutes, stirring often, until soft and lightly browned at the edges.",
    "Return the chicken and any juices to the skillet. Stir for 1 to 2 minutes until the chicken reads 165 F on a thermometer.",
    "Turn off the heat and stir in the lime juice.",
    "Warm the tortillas one at a time in a dry pan over medium heat, about 30 seconds per side, until soft and flexible. Fill each with the chicken mixture and serve."
  ],
